{"message":"I can help with this. Based on the published requirements, the best fit for your $25,000 savings is likely the Gold Account: it earns 5.5% APY, requires a $5,000 opening deposit, and requires a $10,000 ongoing balance. Pairing it with a Green Account checking account adds a 0.75% savings APY boost, for a potential 6.25% APY before any eligible credit-card bonus. Platinum and Diamond Elite savings accounts require substantially higher balances, so they would not fit your stated amount.

The Green Account offers early direct deposit, no overdraft fees, and the strongest documented boost for a feasible savings pairing, though its $22.50 monthly fee is waived only with a $1,350 minimum daily balance. I recommend opening the Green Account first, then the Gold Account, transferring your $25,000, and closing your Light Blue Account afterward. Light Blue closure has a $15 early-closure fee only if it was opened within the last 30 days; it has no notice period, and must have no pending transactions.

Before I access your accounts or make changes, please verify any two of these four fields exactly as they appear on your profile: date of birth, email address, phone number, or mailing address. Also confirm that you want the Green Account and Gold Account combination, and whether you authorize transferring the $25,000 to the new savings account immediately after it is opened."}

